  "query_preview": "..The monsoon is over and a ridge of high pressure \nhas built into the region. This will bring dry conditions with \ntemperatures at or slightly above average during the day and \nseasonably cool at night through the weekend. \n\nModels suggest the possibility of the ridge being briefly\nsuppressed by a shortwave moving through the area. This could\nbring a few showers to the higher elevations Monday and Tuesday \nafternoon but each run has been showing the chances of this \noccurring trending downward so confidence is low on this scenario.\n\nBy the middle to the end of next week high pressure rebounds into\nan even stronger ridge with heights of 588-591dm in the center.\nThis will lead to continued dry conditions with temperatures\nwarming further, up to 5-10 degrees above average.",
